{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>Grammar:</b> הוחל is a pi'el of the doubled [root], and were it not that the ḥet is a guttural, it would have taken a dagesh. It is from the root ח־ל־ל (beginning). The meaning is that they began to pray. Had it been from חול (profanation), the divine name would have been adjacent to the word."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:20.847657501Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}